---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="For QA engineers — Elenkos Systems"
  description="How QA engineers and engineers in test report meaningful bugs, perform blind review, and qualify for flat-rate and commission-linked compensation."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">For engineers</p><h1>Your judgment is part of the product.</h1></div>
    <aside><p>Elenkos is designed for QA engineers and engineers in test who can reproduce, explain, and evaluate failures—not maximize ticket count.</p></aside>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card teal"><p class="kicker">Report</p><h3>Build a case</h3><p>Capture reproducible steps, affected behavior, scope, evidence, environmental conditions, and why the failure matters.</p></article>
      <article class="card amber"><p class="kicker">Review</p><h3>Judge independently</h3><p>When randomly assigned an eligible review, score the report from its allowlisted evidence without access to the AI assessment.</p></article>
      <article class="card red"><p class="kicker">Adjudicate</p><h3>Explain a gap</h3><p>Additional humans may be asked to resolve a material discrepancy. The goal is a reasoned outcome, not forced agreement.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="split">
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">How compensation works</p>
        <h2>Written rates. Review-linked credits.</h2>
        <p>Engagements define a flat rate for assigned work. Reports and blind reviews may also earn credits when the active policy finds meaningful agreement between independent assessments.</p>
        <p>Commission is tied to reviewed seriousness under those terms. It is not a bounty for raw volume, and no score guarantees payment.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">Fairness commitments</p>
        <ul class="signal-list">
          <li>Reviewer assignments use eligibility and conflict exclusions</li>
          <li>The AI score remains sealed until human submission</li>
          <li>Reporter and reviewer can both receive agreement credits</li>
          <li>Material disagreement routes to more humans</li>
          <li>Policy versions and outcomes remain auditable</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="callout">
      <p class="eyebrow">Follow the build</p>
      <h2>The network is not accepting public applications yet.</h2>
      <p>We will publish eligibility, rates, commission terms, privacy rules, and dispute handling before opening participation. Until then, follow the engineering organization for verified launch evidence.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://github.com/elenkos-systems">View Elenkos engineering</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
